    deck: "Shopping and the market",
    body: `
<p>English uses "have" for what you own and "there is / there are" for what exists somewhere. Vietnamese uses one word for both: <b>có</b>.</p>
<h3>có: have</h3>
<p>Person, then <b>có</b>, then the thing. Counted things keep their classifier.</p>
{{ex:Tôi có hai anh trai.|dtohy kaw/ hahy aing chahy|I have two older brothers.}}
{{ex:Chị Lan có một con mèo.|chee. lahn kaw/ moht. kawn mehw_|Lan has a cat.}}
<h3>có: there is, there are</h3>
<p>Say the place first, then <b>có</b>, then what is there. <b>ở đây</b> means "here".</p>
{{ex:Ở đây có wifi.|er? day kaw/ wai fai|There's wifi here.}}
{{ex:Ở Hà Nội có nhiều quán phở.|er? hah_ nohy. kaw/ nyee-uhw_ kwahn/ fer?|There are lots of pho places in Hanoi.}}
<p>When the place is clear from the situation, leave it out and start with <b>có</b>: <b>Có wifi không?</b> is a quick "Is there wifi?" at a café.</p>
<p>English "there is" never becomes <b>là</b>. <b>là</b> joins two nouns ("A is B"); it does not say that something exists.</p>
<h3>không có: don't have, there isn't</h3>
<p>Put <b>không</b> before <b>có</b>, as before any verb.</p>
{{ex:Tôi không có xe máy.|dtohy khohng kaw/ seh mai/|I don't have a motorbike.}}
<h3>Asking: có … không?</h3>
<p>You already ask yes/no questions with <b>có … không</b>. With "have", the <b>có</b> is the verb itself, so the question is simply <b>có</b> + thing + <b>không</b>. This is how you ask in a shop or at a stall.</p>
{{ex:Chị có áo màu đỏ không?|chee. kaw/ ahw/ mow_ daw? khohng|Do you have a red shirt? (to a saleswoman a little older)}}
{{ex:Ở đây có nhà vệ sinh không?|er? day kaw/ nyah_ vey. sing khohng|Is there a restroom here?}}
<p>You can ask about one particular thing too. Keep its classifier and <b>này</b>: <b>Chị có quyển sách này không?</b> (Do you have this book?)</p>
<p>Answer yes with <b>Có</b>. Answer no with <b>Không</b> or <b>Không có</b>. A seller may soften it: <b>Dạ, không có ạ.</b></p>
{{ex:Không có.|khohng kaw/|No, we don't. / No, there isn't.}}
<h3>Not for age</h3>
<p>Don't stretch <b>có</b> to ages. "I'm twenty" is <b>Tôi hai mươi tuổi</b>, with no <b>có</b> and no <b>là</b>.</p>
<div class="tip"><b>Most common mistake:</b> using <b>là</b> for "there is". <b>Ở đây là nhà vệ sinh không?</b> → <b>Ở đây có nhà vệ sinh không?</b></div>
`,
